tacra, attest: no RRP identifier and no server_id in the binding or the bundle, as the group decided on 6 October

The backend computes the Verifier session's nonce with an empty RRP identifier field (the layout of TACRA Section 4.5
kept, so that the identifier can return once the threat model is agreed; TheBankster/rats-tacra#20); the per-RRP switch
omit_rrp_id_in_binding is gone. The test vector is a hardware one: the present-nonce Enrollment of the bench's GCP SEV-SNP
run of 8 October without the identifier (20261008T205230Z-gcp-sev-snp-no-rrp-id), whose REPORT_DATA is this value. The
fork's binding digest and EncryptedCredentialBundle drop server_id: the EST Server is invisible to the Attester
(lamps-tacra-est#10). common.go: the fork's constants block as it was, the attest-* media types in a block of their own
(Mark Novak's review of TWI-Unified-Model/globalsign-est#4, 11 October 2026). The same change as the transfer branch's
commits 4175988 and 7e4224c.

